audio: grow the I2S SRAM ring 32 KiB -> 64 KiB, taking the space from hart0

THREE ARTEFACTS. The memory map lives in the loader, OpenSBI and the kernel,
and all three must agree:

    make bootloader && make opensbi && make linux
    make flash-loader && make flash-opensbi && make flash-linux

Files here are the kernel's two. The third change is
shared/s31_memory_layout.h (S31_AUDIO_DMA_BASE 0x2F062000 -> 0x2F05A000,
S31_AUDIO_DMA_SIZE 0x8000 -> 0x10000), which is in the repo proper.

WHY
What the ring holds is TIME, and time is bytes divided by rate. At 16 KiB per
stream that is 372 ms at 11025 but only 93 ms at 44100 - and a frame dip
longer than the ring underruns, which is heard as a crackle. lvdesk's frame
gaps under Doom run 100-400 ms. That is why 11025 is clean and 44100 is not:
not the codec, not the plugin, just arithmetic.

    rate     16 KiB    32 KiB
    11025    372 ms    743 ms
    22050    186 ms    372 ms
    44100     93 ms    186 ms

Verified on the board: BUFFER_SIZE went from [256 4096] to [256 8192], and a
44100 stream now reports buffer_size 8184.

WHERE THE MEMORY CAME FROM
It has to be uncached internal SRAM - PSRAM is cached on this SoC and the
GDMA would read stale samples - and the hosted Wi-Fi transport ring sits
3,968 bytes above the pool, so the only direction is down, into hart0's heap.

rootfs/s31_freertos_mem.c (built now, was not) asks hart0 for its internal
DMA-capable heap over the existing hosted-sram ioctl:

                          before      after
    Total heap           222,592    189,824
    Historical min free   60,456     36,344
    Verdict                 PASS       PASS

The historical minimum is the honest number - the worst ever observed with
the radios running - so 32 KiB was affordable and 48 KiB would not have been.
35.5 KiB of margin remains. IF WI-FI OR BLUETOOTH START MISBEHAVING, SUSPECT
THIS FIRST.

THE LOADER IS NOT OPTIONAL. main.c reserves [S31_AUDIO_DMA_BASE,
LINUX_SRAM_START) from the ESP-IDF heap allocator. A stale loader fences off
the OLD base, so hart0's heap would allocate inside Linux's DMA ring: silent
corruption, not a boot failure.

TOOLING NOTE. make flash-bootloader shells out to idf.py and cannot work on
this host - no host-side ESP-IDF has an esp32s31 target, the S31-capable one
is v6.1-dev inside the build container. make flash-loader was added to do it
with $(ESPFLASH) like every other flash target, offset read from
partitions.csv.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT FIX
A dip longer than 186 ms still underruns, and the worst frame measured today
was 386 ms. This halves the problem; it does not remove it. The unbounded
version is rings in PSRAM via the hart0 transport, with everything that
implies (see docs/current-state.md).
